  AN ANALYTIC CHECK OF THE WHOLE CONSTRUCTION, so the band is not one solver's opinion.
  Writing Psi(g) = nu(g) g (= g_obs/a0), the two evaluation points collapse to
      near = Psi(y-e) + Psi(e),   far = Psi(y+e) - Psi(e)      [exact, any kernel]
  so to first order in e the dipole is   A_v = [ Psi(e) - e Psi'(y) ] / Psi(y).
  [OK] the symbolic first-order law reproduces the numeric Route A dipole to 0.42% on all four v3 cells -- an INDEPENDENT derivation of the same band, and it exhibits why the dipole exists at all: nu is nonlinear, so Psi(e) does not cancel e Psi'(y)

