============================================================================================================
S8. (d) DOES 'PURE MI PREDICTS EXACTLY ZERO' STILL HOLD? -- Newtonian control, both roads
============================================================================================================
  [OK] CONTROL: with nu == 1 (Newton) the MI quadrature gives ZERO on all 19 cells -- exactly 0.0 in 18 of them and at most 2.0e-16 in the rest. It is ANALYTICALLY identically zero (near = (y-e)+e and far = (y+e)-e are the same number), and the residual 2.0e-16 is float64 cancellation in e-(e-y) at the e >> y cells, six to nine orders below any physical value in the tables above. So the dipole is owned by the NONLINEARITY of nu and by nothing else
  [OK] CONTROL, second road: with nu == 1 the phantom density vanishes identically and the BVP returns exactly 0.0 in all 20 cells. Both constructions agree that the dipole is a pure nonlinearity effect
  [OK] THEREFORE the answer to (d) is: 'pure MI predicts EXACTLY ZERO' is NOT restored by Route A. The exponential kernel is nonlinear, so the corpus's own Theorem 5 construction gives 4.4-20.5% under it, exactly as it gave 4.2-22.3% under alpha=1 and 5.4-15.4% under alpha=2. This is not new: mi_efe_derived_general_2026 already RETIRED that banked line. What IS newly verified is that the retirement is KERNEL-INDEPENDENT -- it is a statement about MI's nonlinearity and about which realization is asked, and the shape of the approach to Newton cannot bring the zero back. NB the surviving 'can vanish for pure MI' caveat in laneA is a different claim (a strictly uniform g_ext as a pure frame acceleration); that is a REALIZATION fork, untouched here and untouched by Route A

